Title      : clk_sys falling edge as its own clock (CLK_MID)
Project    : fpga-mister (patch for SNES_MiSTer bdcd33c, after 0001)
Author     : Konstantin Schmidt (mr_pleasant@gmx.de)
Company    : OHRZ
Created    : 2026-10-30
Description:
  On the Zynq the core clocks are pulses of the gated master clock (BUFGCE):
  clk_sys is high for one master high time (5.6 ns), not half its period
  (23 ns on the DE10).  Logic at the falling edge of clk_sys got 5.6 ns from
  the rising edge (Vivado WNS -5.1 ns).  The core profile adds CLK_MID, a
  pulse at the master pulse where the DE10 clk_sys falls (the 2nd clk_mem
  pulse of every clk_sys period, cores/snes/pll.vhd), and every falling
  edge of clk_sys becomes a rising edge of CLK_MID:
    CEGen (DSP, DSP_LHRomMap, CX4Map; msu_audio by rules.py), the four
    falling-edge processes and the cache RAM of GSU, the two RAMs of CX4
    (clock => not CLK).
  The order of all edges stays as on the DE10, also while the core is
  stalled.  New ports CLK_MID/MCLK_MID/DSPCLK_MID, wired by rules.py in
  rtl/main.v and SNES.sv.
  One line of context (git diff -U1): prepare_sources.py rewrites the .mif
  path in the line before the CX4 DATA_ROM clock.
diff --git a/rtl/CEGen.vhd b/rtl/CEGen.vhd
index 37d74c4..62b50f3 100644
--- a/rtl/CEGen.vhd
+++ b/rtl/CEGen.vhd
@@ -24,3 +24,3 @@ BEGIN
 			CE <= '0';
-		elsif falling_edge(CLK) then
+		elsif rising_edge(CLK) then
 			CE <= '0';
diff --git a/rtl/DSP.vhd b/rtl/DSP.vhd
index 11e86c0..2f33700 100644
--- a/rtl/DSP.vhd
+++ b/rtl/DSP.vhd
@@ -11,2 +11,3 @@ entity DSP is
 		CLK 			: in std_logic;
+		CLK_MID		: in std_logic;  -- fpga-mister: clk_sys falling edge as its own clock
 		RST_N 		: in std_logic; 
@@ -243,3 +244,3 @@ begin
 	port map(
-		CLK      => CLK,
+		CLK      => CLK_MID,
 		RST_N    => CEGEN_RST_N,
